# NOTE on where Docker actually reads this file from:
#
# Agent/docker/Dockerfile needs to COPY Agent/backend/ and
# Agent/requirements.txt, and Docker refuses any COPY source that resolves
# outside the build context via "..". That forces docker-compose.yml's build
# context to be Agent/ (one level up from this docker/ directory), not
# Agent/docker/ itself. Docker's *automatic* .dockerignore discovery only
# ever looks at "<context>/.dockerignore" -- i.e. Agent/.dockerignore -- so
# this file, kept at the path this deployment package documents everything
# else at, is NOT automatically picked up by a plain `docker compose build`.
#
# That is not a security gap: Agent/docker/Dockerfile's own COPY list is an
# explicit ALLOW-list (only requirements.txt and backend/), never a wildcard
# "COPY . .", so nothing below can leak into the image regardless of whether
# this particular file is "wired up" by Docker itself. This file is a second,
# human-reviewable line of defence -- and doubles as the exact list an
# operator can `ln -sf docker/.dockerignore Agent/.dockerignore` (see
# Agent/docker/README.md) to also get the minor, purely cosmetic benefit of
# Docker skipping these paths when it uploads the build context.

# Bot ledgers/candle cache/analysis output -- 260MB+ of runtime data that is
# never baked into the image; mounted from the host instead (data read-only,
# cache/candles read-write) -- see docker-compose.yml.
data/

# Secrets: OKX API key/secret/passphrase. Loaded into the container as real
# environment variables via docker-compose's `env_file:` at `docker compose
# up` time -- the file itself must never be copied into the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Version control, caches, editor/tooling cruft.
.git/
.gitignore
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo

# Test suite -- not needed to run the service, and its fixtures duplicate
# real bot data under test-only paths.
test/

# Human-facing docs, plans, generated reports, ad-hoc run logs -- none of
# this is needed to run the service.
docs/
plan.md
README.md
log/

# One-off crawler/maintenance scripts -- not imported by Agent.backend.web.*,
# not needed at runtime.
scripts/

# This docker/ directory is the tooling that builds/runs the image; it is
# never needed *inside* the image itself.
docker/
deploy/
